    "section": "02. Datasheets",
    "ruleNumber": "02.02.01",
    "parent": {
      "kind": "core-rule",
      "id": "profiles"
    },
    "summary": "A modifier is a rule that changes a roll, a characteristic or another value, which is then ‘modified’. A +N improves a characteristic by N and a -N worsens it by N.\n\nAll modifiers stack. Modify a value, such as a characteristic, dice roll or distance, in this order:\n\n1. Change or replace it with any value a rule sets; a characteristic set to ‘0’, ‘-’ or an asterisk this way takes no further modifiers (skip steps 2 to 5).\n2. Multiply.\n3. Add.\n4. Divide.\n5. Subtract.\n6. Round fractions up.\n\nUnless stated otherwise, characteristics of ‘-’, an asterisk or ‘N/A’ are never modified, changing a model’s **WS** or **BS** changes it on every weapon the model has, and after all modifiers:\n\n- **M** and **Range** are at least 1\".\n- **T**, **A**, **S** and **D** are at least 1.\n- **Sv** and **InSv** are no better than 2+.\n- **Ld** is between 5+ and 8+.\n- **OC** is at least 0 and can’t become ‘-’.\n- **WS** and **BS** are between 2+ and 6+.\n- **AP** is 0 at worst.\n\nImproving and worsening:\n\n- **WS**, **BS**, **Sv** and **Ld**: improving lowers the number before the ‘+’ by the amount, and worsening raises it.\n- **AP**: improving subtracts the amount, and reducing or worsening adds it, but never past 0.\n- Characteristics without a ‘+’ or ‘-’: improving adds the amount, and worsening subtracts it.\n\nFor dice rolls:\n\n- Modify after any re-rolls; an ‘unmodified’ roll is the result after re-rolls and before modifiers.\n- A result may be modified beyond the die’s highest face, such as above 6 on a D6; one below 1 becomes 1.\n- A **hit roll** or **wound roll** takes a net modifier of at most +1 or -1: a total of -2 or worse counts as -1, and +2 or better as +1.\n- A **charge roll** result of 13 or more becomes 12.\n\nOther limits after all modifiers:\n\n- **Detection range** and **[Lone Operative](vsdata:core-ability/lone-operative)** stay between 9\" and 30\".\n- A Stratagem’s CP cost rises by at most 1 and never drops below 0.",
